From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:54:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: listen on vsock alone when the launch has no host
 forward

adbd listens on TCP and vsock port 5555 by default. A launch with no
host forward (the iOS release) lets nothing outside the guest reach that
TCP listener, so it serves only the guest's own applications: one could
raise adbd's authorization prompt, and on a userdebug build an accepted
key gets a shell that reaches su. The host application reaches adbd over
virtio-vsock instead.

The launch passes ro.boot.kernarium.adb_tcp, 0 when it has no host
forward. When service.adb.listen_addrs is empty and that property is
false, adbd now listens on vsock:5555 alone. Without the property, or
with any other value, the addresses are what they were.

adbd reads the policy itself, as it reads ro.boot.kernarium.adb_auth:
the property is a bootloader_prop that every domain may read, whereas
service.adb.listen_addrs is a system_prop that vendor_init may not set,
so neither SELinux nor init changes.
---
 daemon/main.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/daemon/main.cpp b/daemon/main.cpp
index 757020ac84323c6bf192100e01249d45eaa77c92..7a54ae487b5d8ba6acbfb73969a0e1a1634d1c3f 100644
--- a/daemon/main.cpp
+++ b/daemon/main.cpp
@@ -278,6 +278,12 @@ int adbd_main() {
     // on the default port.
     std::vector<std::string> addrs;
     std::string prop_addr = android::base::GetProperty("service.adb.listen_addrs", "");
+    // A launch with no host forward sets ro.boot.kernarium.adb_tcp to 0: the host application then
+    // reaches adbd over vsock alone, and no application of the guest finds a TCP listener. Without
+    // the property, or with any other value, adbd listens where it always did.
+    if (prop_addr.empty() && !android::base::GetBoolProperty("ro.boot.kernarium.adb_tcp", true)) {
+        prop_addr = android::base::StringPrintf("vsock:%d", DEFAULT_ADB_LOCAL_TRANSPORT_PORT);
+    }
     if (prop_addr.empty()) {
         std::string prop_port = android::base::GetProperty("service.adb.tcp.port", "");
         if (prop_port.empty()) {
